## Context

Phase 2 ablation (PR #250) has three confounded variables: temperature
(null vs 0.0), RAG document presence (72K vs 350K tokens), and prompt
module content. The experiment cannot cleanly attribute ΔF1 to prompt
modules because replicates are not comparable.

16/32 DeepSeek runs are refusals caused by over-context prompts
(353K-377K tokens vs 163K context window), not by prompt content.

## Actions

1. After ticket 0094 fixes the injection inconsistency, re-run all 64
   calls: 16 variants × 2 models × 2 reps.
2. All runs must use: temperature=0.0, RAG documents included, same
   corpus (18 docs, ~37K tokens).
3. If DeepSeek still refuses at 350K+ tokens, consider: (a) truncating
   the RAG corpus to fit within 163K, or (b) replacing DeepSeek with a
   model that handles over-context gracefully.
4. Rebuild measurements.jsonl and verify no token count variance between
   replicates.

## Test

All 64 records in measurements.jsonl have consistent token counts
(within 5%) across replicates of the same variant+model.

## Exit criteria

- 64 clean measurements with consistent settings
- No temperature=null entries in Phase 2 data
- ΔF1 per module computable without confounds
